</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula>B signalling and reduces inflammatory cytokine production in aging</article-title><source><italic>The Journal of Biological Chemistry</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>273</volume><issue>49</issue><fpage>32833</fpage><lpage>32841</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9830030</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B92"><label>91</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Masoro</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Overview of caloric restriction and ageing</article-title><source><italic>Mechanisms of Ageing and Development</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>126</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>913</fpage><lpage>922</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15885745</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B93"><label>92</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Erol</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>PPAR&#x003b1;<inline-formula><mml:math id="M27"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>&#x003b1;</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula>activators may be good candidates as antiaging agents</article-title><source><italic>Medical Hypotheses</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>65</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>35</fpage><lpage>38</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15893114</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B94"><label>93</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guarente</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Picard</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Calorie restriction-the SIR2 connection</article-title><source><italic>Cell</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>120</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>473</fpage><lpage>482</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15734680</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B95"><label>94</label><citation citation-type="journa